questions.expected:
A strong answer separates bundled payload installation from remote payload fetching and avoids classifying ordinary installers as malicious without suspicious context.

```pseudocode
function classifyExecutable(events):
    wroteExecutable = false
    launchedChildExecutable = false
    fetchedRemotePayload = false
    suspiciousInstallPath = false

    for event in events:
        if event.type == "$file_write$" and event.extension in ["exe", "dll", "sys", "ps1"]:
            wroteExecutable = true
            if event.path contains "Temp" or event.path contains "AppData" or event.path contains "Startup":
                suspiciousInstallPath = true

        if event.type == "$process_start$" and event.parent == events.subjectProcess:
            if event.imagePath was written by events.subjectProcess:
                launchedChildExecutable = true

        if event.type == "$network_download$":
            if event.responseContentType in ["application/octet-stream", "application/x-msdownload"]:
                fetchedRemotePayload = true

    if fetchedRemotePayload and wroteExecutable and launchedChildExecutable:
        return "likely downloader"

    if wroteExecutable and launchedChildExecutable and suspiciousInstallPath:
        return "likely dropper"

    return "neither or insufficient evidence"
```
